{:theorem
 {:id :theorem,
  :statement
  "Let $f: \\{0,1\\}^n \\to \\{+1,-1\\}$ be any Boolean function. Let $L_f$ be its diagonal observable and $\\tilde{L}_f = \\mathcal{U}(L_f) = T^{\\otimes n} H^{\\otimes n} L_f H^{\\otimes n} (T^{\\otimes n})^\\dagger$. Then: (i) $H(\\tilde{L}_f) = H(L_f) + \\mathrm{Inf}(L_f) = H(f) + \\mathrm{Inf}(f)$, (ii) $\\mathrm{Inf}(\\tilde{L}_f) = \\mathrm{Inf}(L_f) = \\mathrm{Inf}(f)$, (iii) $\\frac{H(\\tilde{L}_f)}{\\mathrm{Inf}(\\tilde{L}_f)} = \\frac{H(f)}{\\mathrm{Inf}(f)} + 1$.",
  :content-hash "4a4ba22f0fa7e137"},
 :obligations [],
 :archived-nodes {},
 :external-refs {},
 :nodes
 {:1-t1a002
  {:statement
   "**Part (ii): Influence invariance.** The transformation $\\mathcal{U} = T^{\\otimes n} H^{\\otimes n}$ is a product unitary, being a tensor product of single-qubit gates $T H$ on each qubit.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "27910f64f33306aa",
   :display-order 2,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-t1a002,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-t1a001}},
  :1-t1a010
  {:statement
   "By Lemma 6: $H(\\tilde{L}_f) = H(L_f) + \\sum_S \\pi(X_S) \\log_2 k_S = H(L_f) + \\sum_S \\hat{f}(S)^2 \\log_2(2^{|S|}) = H(L_f) + \\sum_S \\hat{f}(S)^2 \\cdot |S| = H(L_f) + \\mathrm{Inf}(f)$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "fa0a3e262cddadb6",
   :display-order 10,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :substitution,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-t1a010,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-t1a009}},
  :1-t1a007
  {:statement
   "The Pauli spectral distribution after Hadamard is $\\pi(X_S) = \\hat{f}(S)^2$ - the distribution is the same as before (just relabeled $Z_S \\to X_S$). Hence $H(H^{\\otimes n} L_f (H^{\\otimes n})^\\dagger) = H(L_f) = H(f)$ (entropy unchanged by relabeling).",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "d5def66e7ff01327",
   :display-order 7,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-t1a007,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-t1a006}},
  :1-t1a001
  {:statement
   "Let $f: \\{0,1\\}^n \\to \\{+1,-1\\}$ be a Boolean function. By Lemma 1, $L_f = \\sum_{S \\subseteq [n]} \\hat{f}(S) Z_S$ is the Pauli expansion of the diagonal observable.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "0326328e6665c32a",
   :display-order 1,
   :type :assumption,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :assumption,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-t1a001,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{}},
  :1-t1a012
  {:statement
   "**Part (iii): Ratio increase.** From Parts (i) and (ii): $\\frac{H(\\tilde{L}_f)}{\\mathrm{Inf}(\\tilde{L}_f)} = \\frac{H(f) + \\mathrm{Inf}(f)}{\\mathrm{Inf}(f)} = \\frac{H(f)}{\\mathrm{Inf}(f)} + 1$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "8ac81501f6308908",
   :display-order 12,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
